{"parentUuid":"a0beae32-4368-495f-90a4-6dfafc05096d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01TPv3q8WaTNWreXUnLRKNkW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good instinct — measure before committing to ~500 lines of daemon code. Here's a concrete benchmark plan.\n\n## What we'd measure\n\nWe want one number: **cold-start overhead per `opf` invocation**. The daemon win equals exactly that. Inference itself is the same either way.\n\n## Benchmark plan (~1–2 hours of work, mostly waiting on installs)\n\n1. **Install OPF locally** — clone `openai/privacy-filter`, `pip install -e .`, let it download weights to `~/.opf/privacy_filter` on first run (~1.5 GB, one-time)\n2. **Pick a representative input** — reuse the existing fixture `cmd/entire/cli/transcript/compact/testdata/claude_full2.jsonl` so numbers line up with `BenchmarkRedactJSONLBytes`\n3. **Three measurements:**\n   - **Cold shell-out:** `time opf -f claude_full2.jsonl`, run 3 times in fresh shells, take median\n   - **Warm in-process:** a 30-line Python script that imports `opf._api`, loads model once, then redacts the same fixture 5 times in a loop. Time per call after the first.\n   - **Pure Python startup:** `time python -c 'import opf'` for a sanity-check on how much is Python import overhead vs. model load\n4. **Decision rule:**\n   - If `cold − warm` > ~2s **and** you expect frequent condensations per session → daemon pays off\n   - If `cold − warm` < ~500ms → shell-out is fine, daemon is busywork\n   - In between → judgment call; lean shell-out for shipping speed\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- Crucially, **the runtime choice is decoupled from every other part of this design.** Settings schema, integration point (condensation + export), category defaults, failure mode, replacement tokens — none of those depend on shell-out vs daemon. So we don't need to resolve this before continuing the design. We resolve it before writing the runtime adapter.\n- The benchmark itself isn't code we ship — it's a research probe to inform a single design knob. We can run it on your laptop or a representative dev machine; numbers from CI runners would be misleading because they're often slower than dev machines.\n- A useful third data point: time the *entire current condensation* end-to-end on a real session (no OPF) to know how big the latency budget is. If condensation already takes 800ms today, adding 2s of OPF cold-start *triples* it; adding 200ms is noise. Context matters more than raw numbers.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3898,"cache_read_input_tokens":123815,"output_tokens":2860,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3898,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2860,"cache_read_input_tokens":123815,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3898,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3898},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CayeD8z6R37Z48enV83xv","type":"assistant","uuid":"f4be3db6-fe69-46aa-8753-b60887eb9c4c","timestamp":"2026-05-13T00:44:51.047Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact","sessionId":"fb93c4d8-9548-4a4c-97e6-364245c50453","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"openai-redact"}
