{"parentUuid":"ed8b3ca7-c1d3-4e66-a9ca-89eb7a67ddcd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01UCjB89xcLh1VM32tGVXXSY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good — there's already `RedactionSettings { PII, CustomRedactions }` in `settings/settings.go:159`. OPF fits as a sibling field with no disruption to existing config.\n\n---\n\n### Section 2 — Settings schema\n\nA new optional field on `RedactionSettings`, parallel to `PII`:\n\n```jsonc\n// .entire/settings.json\n{\n  \"redaction\": {\n    \"pii\":               { /* existing, unchanged */ },\n    \"custom_redactions\": { /* existing, unchanged */ },\n\n    \"openai_privacy_filter\": {\n      \"enabled\": false,                       // master switch; default off\n      \"categories\": {                         // per-category opt-in; all default false\n        \"private_person\":   true,             // <- the recommended default\n        \"private_email\":    false,\n        \"private_phone\":    false,\n        \"private_address\":  false,\n        \"private_url\":      false,\n        \"private_date\":     false,\n        \"secret\":           false,\n        \"account_number\":   false\n      },\n      \"command\":         \"opf\",               // override if not on PATH or pinned to a venv\n      \"timeout_seconds\": 30,                  // per-call hard timeout\n      \"on_failure\":      \"warn\"               // \"warn\" | \"block\"; default \"warn\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe Go struct mirroring it lives in `settings/settings.go`:\n\n```go\ntype RedactionSettings struct {\n    PII                  *PIISettings              `json:\"pii,omitempty\"`\n    CustomRedactions     map[string]string         `json:\"custom_redactions,omitempty\"`\n    OpenAIPrivacyFilter  *OPFSettings              `json:\"openai_privacy_filter,omitempty\"`\n}\n\ntype OPFSettings struct {\n    Enabled        bool            `json:\"enabled\"`\n    Categories     map[string]bool `json:\"categories,omitempty\"`\n    Command        string          `json:\"command,omitempty\"`         // default \"opf\"\n    TimeoutSeconds int             `json:\"timeout_seconds,omitempty\"` // default 30\n    OnFailure      string          `json:\"on_failure,omitempty\"`      // default \"warn\"\n}\n```\n\n**Key design choices, justified:**\n\n- **Settings.json (committed), not settings.local.json.** The redaction *policy* is a team decision; install state is per-machine. The `\"warn\"` default protects devs who haven't run `pip install opf` — they see a warning, condensation proceeds with the existing layers, push works. The existing settings-merge already allows per-machine override via `.entire/settings.local.json` if a user wants to set `\"enabled\": false` locally.\n- **Category strings match OPF's output labels exactly** (`private_person`, not `person`). This means `grep private_person` shows you both the config and the OPF output that produces matches. Same precedent as PII keying off OpenAI's own taxonomy where possible.\n- **`enabled: false` by default**, plus `private_person: true` inside `categories`. So just adding the block does nothing; the user must also flip `enabled`. Two-step opt-in matches the \"optional add-on\" framing.\n- **`command` lets users pin to a venv** (e.g., `/Users/alice/.venvs/opf/bin/opf`) without polluting PATH. Useful for teams that don't want OPF binaries floating around globally.\n- **`on_failure` is the safety knob.** Default `\"warn\"` matches your \"fall back to full existing stack\" direction. Teams that need strict guarantees can set `\"block\"`.\n- **No environment variable override.** All knobs go through settings to keep the precedence story simple. (Existing PII config also has no env overrides.)\n\n**Discovery surface (`entire configure --opf`):** A small interactive flow that:\n1. Checks if `opf` is on PATH; prints install instructions if not\n2. Walks through the categories with descriptions\n3. Writes the result to `.entire/settings.json`\n\nThis mirrors the existing `entire configure` pattern. Not strictly required for v1 — users could hand-edit the JSON — but it removes friction for the default case.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- Putting OPF settings under existing `RedactionSettings` means **zero new top-level config keys**. The whole feature lives behind one nested object that's invisible until the user adds it. Backward-compatible by construction.\n- Storing categories as `map[string]bool` instead of struct fields with `*bool` (like `PIISettings.Email`) is intentional: OPF's taxonomy could grow (the README hints at fine-tuning to add new labels). A map handles new categories without a settings.go change.\n- The `command` field is a small UX win we should *not* skip. Without it, the failure message on macOS is \"opf not found\" and the user has to figure out that pyenv put it in `~/.pyenv/shims/opf`. With it, the install-instructions message can say \"if `opf` isn't on PATH, set `command` to its full path.\"\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nSound right, or do you want to push back on anything — settings location, category list naming, the `command` field, the two-step opt-in?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1050,"cache_read_input_tokens":132832,"output_tokens":1833,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1050,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1833,"cache_read_input_tokens":132832,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1050,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1050},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CayeJFH1B1p5gDB9y92DG","type":"assistant","uuid":"74d48b95-6d1a-4489-9149-50835226e503","