etuning_secret_demo](https://github.com/openai/privacy-filter/blob/main/examples/data/finetuning_secret_demo))","+reframes the `secret` and `account_number` categories. The three public","+`secret` examples (`sk-test-XYZ987`, `Priv4cy-Filt3r-2026`,","+`QK-TST-000-BDX5YNAL`) and the single public `account_number` example","+(`40702810500001234567`) all appear in **conversational context** —","+\"rotate secret …\", \"passphrase …\", \"send a bill for account …\", \"marker","+…\". The model is keying off the surrounding human prose, not raw entropy.","+This is **complementary** to betterleaks (which detects credentials by","+shape) rather than redundant: OPF's `secret` is most useful for opaque","+values that humans *talked about* in transcripts but that don't match a","+known credential format. The model card's documented failure mode","+(over-redaction of benign high-entropy strings, hashes, placeholders) is","+still real, but the surface where OPF *over*-fires is the same surface","+where our entropy and betterleaks layers *already* fire — the merge","+machinery collapses overlapping regions to a single redaction. Net: the","+risk profile of enabling `secret` is bounded, but precision against real","+transcripts is the gating question and is measured in the benchmark","+phase before recommending any change to defaults.","+"," ### Constraints carried from prior incidents"," "," - **Over-redaction makes logs unusable.** Prior versions of the redaction"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5c974ef8-c834-4ef0-b1a2-433ca4197a39","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact","sessionId":"fb93c4d8-9548-4a4c-97e6-364245c50453","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"openai-redact"}
