t and then unconditionally writes `dst.Enabled = override.Enabled` — meaning a settings.local.json that mentions `openai_privacy_filter` but doesn't include `\"enabled\"` will silently flip `Enabled` to `false`. The plan's own `TestLoadFromBytes_OpenAIPrivacyFilter_Merge` test would fail to detect this because the test doesn't exercise the \"field absent\" case. Fix: rewrite `mergeOPFSettings` to use the `map[string]json.RawMessage` pattern, matching `mergePIISettings`.\n\n- **[Task 8, file list]:** The migration list enumerates `committed.go:264` (JSONLBytes) but omits `committed.go:270` (`agentContent = redact.Bytes(agentContent)`) and `committed.go:1778, :1783` (more `redact.Bytes(content)` fallbacks). The two `Bytes` calls live in the same condensation paths as their `JSONLBytes` siblings and need to migrate together. The plan also doesn't add `BytesWithPrivacyFilter` to the redact package until Task 9 Step 1, but Task 8 already needs it. Either move `BytesWithPrivacyFilter` to Task 6 (with the other entry points) or expand Task 8's file list. The verification command at the end of the plan (`git grep -nE 'redact\\.(JSONLBytes|String|Bytes|JSONLContent)\\('`) would catch this, but only after the chunk is already committed.\n\n- **[Task 7]:** The progress UX writer (`progressWriter.Start`/`Finish`) is defined and tested in Task 7, but no step actually invokes it on the success path. `detectOPF` is never modified to call `Start`/`Finish` around the `cfg.runtime.Redact(...)` call, and no caller passes a `progressWriter` in. The success \"→ scanning transcript / ✓ done (1.8s)\" lines documented in the spec will therefore never appear. Either remove the success-path progress UX from scope or add a step that wires `newProgressWriter(os.Stderr, interactive.IsTerminalWriter(os.Stderr), accessibleEnv())` into `detectOPF` (or `*WithPrivacyFilter`).\n\n- **[Task 6, Step 4 note]:** \"Refactor `JSONLContent` to accept a `func(string) string`\" understates the work. `JSONLContent` calls `String(line)` directly at `redact.go:543` for the parse-fallback path, and the JSON walker `collectJSONLReplacements` at `redact.go:665` calls `String(val)` directly. Threading a function parameter through both paths is doable but the plan reads as if it's a single-line change. Add a substep that enumerates the two callsites in `redact.go` that need the function threaded through, or restructure `collectJSONLReplacements` to take a string-fn argument.\n\n**Recommendations (advisory):**\n\n- **[Task 2, Step 3]:** Stub-now-implement-later inside `redact/opf_runtime/runtime.go` works but the plan then asks Task 4 Step 5 to \"remove the old stub\" — this is two passes over the same file. Consider creating `runtime.go` (just interface + types + factory signature, no impl) in Chunk 1 and `shellout.go` with the real impl in Chunk 2, so neither pass has to delete code the previous pass added.\n\n- **[Task 2, `TestGetOPFConfig_DefaultNil`]:** The test is explicitly noted as \"informational at this stage\" and uses `t.Logf` instead of an assertion. A test that never fails is noise; either tighten it now or drop it.\n\n- **[Task 6, `TestStringWithPrivacyFilter_RegionsMergeWithEntropy`]:** The hard-coded entropy claim `\"Zk83x7Pq2Lm9Vn4Jr1Tw\" // entropy ~ 4.6` is fragile — entropy thresholds drift. Either compute the entropy in the test setup with `secretPattern` directly or use a known-fixture string already validated by the existing entropy tests.\n\n- **[Task 4, Step 4 NOTE]:** \"verify the actual flag name against `opf redact --help` during implementation. If the flag does not exist with that exact name, swap to the correct one\" — this is fine as a NOTE, but it means the wire format in `shellout.go` is unverified until the implementer has `opf` installed. Consider moving the live-binary check to *before* writing the adapter, or capturing a real `opf --help` transcript in the spec.\n\n- **[Verification checklist]:** Add an explicit \"ran `mise run lint` *after* `mise run fmt`\" step per CLAUDE.md — the chunk-end steps say `mise run fmt && mise run lint` once, but CLAUDE.md specifies a re-lint after any fmt reformatting.\n\n**Files referenced:**\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go:352` (EnsureRedactionConfigured signature)\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go:556-583` (mergeRedaction + mergePIISettings pattern)\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/redact/redact.go:510, :543, :665` (JSONLContent + collectJSONLReplacements call sites)\n- `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go:270, :1778, :1783` (missing `redact.Bytes` migrations)"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a827a9a848acfe574 (use SendMessage with to: 'a827a9a848acfe574' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 97911\ntool_uses: 29\nduration_ms: 118615</usage>"}]}]},"uuid":"9424e3b4-9fe8-4bed-8551-9f98f33a068b","timestamp":"2026-05-13T16:43:19.318Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are a plan document reviewer. Verify this implementation plan is complete and ready for execution.\n\n**Plan to review:** /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-13-openai-privacy-filter-addon.md\n\n**Spec for reference:** /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-12-openai-privacy-filter-addon-design.md\n\nCodebase context to check claims against:\n- `redact/redact.go` (existing detector with layers 1-7, merge machinery at lines 235-265)\n- `redact/pii.go`, `redact/custom.go`, `redact/packs.go` (existing layers)\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go:159` (RedactionSettings struct)\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go:556` (mergeRedaction function)\n- `cmd/entire/cli/s