ible progress messages, failure-message formatter\n- `redact/opf_runtime/` (subpackage) — Runtime interface, Span type, shell-out impl with dependency-injected CommandRunner\n\n**New entry points in `redact`:**\n- `StringWithPrivacyFilter(ctx, s) string`\n- `JSONLContentWithPrivacyFilter(ctx, content) (string, error)`\n- `JSONLBytesWithPrivacyFilter(ctx, b) (RedactedBytes, error)`\n- `BytesWithPrivacyFilter(ctx, b) []byte`\n\n**Settings extension:**\n- `RedactionSettings.OpenAIPrivacyFilter *OPFSettings` (sibling to PII/CustomRedactions)\n\n**Strategy wire-up:**\n- `loadAndApplyRedactionSettings()` extracted from `EnsureRedactionConfigured`'s sync.Once body, calls `redact.ConfigurePrivacyFilter(...)` from settings\n\n**Callsite migration:**\n- All condensation callsites in strategy/manual_commit_*.go and checkpoint/{committed,v2_committed}.go switched to `*WithPrivacyFilter`\n- Export callsites in attach.go, explain.go, doctor_bundle.go switched\n- temporary.go (per-turn writes) intentionally left on plain entry points with explanatory comment\n- migrate.go untouched (uses AlreadyRedacted)\n\n## What to Review\n\nWhole-feature concerns:\n\n1. **API coherence:** Are all 4 new `*WithPrivacyFilter` entry points consistent in shape (ctx first, same return types as plain siblings, behavior when OPF disabled = identical to plain)?\n2. **Test-seam pollution:** `GetOPFConfigForTest` and `ResetOPFConfigForTest` are in production code (necessary because `*_test.go` files can't cross packages). Are the docstrings sufficiently strong? Is there any risk a production caller could accidentally use them?\n3. **Settings → runtime config wiring:** Does the configuration path correctly carry through every field? `OPFSettings.TimeoutSeconds` → `OPFConfig.Timeout`?\n4. **Failure-mode coverage:** When `opf` is missing, when it times out, when it returns garbled JSON, when `on_failure: \"block\"` is set — is there a clean code path for each? Are user-facing messages consistent?\n5. **Per-turn write isolation:** Is there ANY production callsite outside `temporary.go` and `migrate.go` that still uses the plain entry points? If so, that's a bug (regression in OPF coverage). Run the verification grep from the plan.\n6. **Concurrent safety:** OPF config global is guarded by RWMutex. detectOPF reads the config under RLock then calls cfg.runtime.Redact without holding the lock. Is there a race window where the runtime could be re-configured mid-call? Acceptable given test pattern?\n7. **Resource cleanup:** Does anything leak across calls? The shell-out runtime spawns a process per call but Close() is no-op (correct for per-call lifecycle).\n8. **Cosmetic:** commit count is 7 (4 feature + 3 followups). The pattern \"chunk feature + small fix\" is intentional. Worth flagging for squash before PR or fine as-is for review traceability.\n\nRun:\n```bash\nmise run check\ngo test ./redact/... ./cmd/entire/cli/... -count=1\ngit grep -nE 'redact\\.(JSONLBytes|String|Bytes|JSONLContent)\\(' cmd/entire/cli/strategy/ cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_committed.go cmd/entire/cli/attach.go cmd/entire/cli/explain.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go\n```\n\n## Reference\n\nSpec: `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-12-openai-privacy-filter-addon-design.md`\nPlan: `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-13-openai-privacy-filter-addon.md`\n\n## Output Format\n\n**Strengths:**\n\n**Issues:**\n- Critical:\n- Important:\n- Minor:\n\n**Assessment:** Ready to merge | Approved-with-followups | Issues-block-merge\n\n**Pre-PR checklist verification:**\n- mise run check passes: yes/no\n- No stray plain callsites in condensation/export: yes/no\n- Spec data-flow audit honored (per-turn untouched): yes/no\n- All 4 entry points behave consistently: yes/no\n- Failure modes produce actionable messages: yes/no\n"},"caller"