{"parentUuid":"4f107be7-0135-41ca-8ccc-2ddc0db05f0d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01PeqwZ4qTq7foLkHU5nwXy4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Honest report — what we actually learned\n\nI was wrong about the Vogon hang being OPF-caused. But running a controlled perf probe surfaced **two real issues**:\n\n### What the gate-enabled probe showed\n\nBefore I killed it, the probe ran against the 1.1MB `claude_full2.jsonl` fixture and produced:\n\n- **1,505 stderr lines** = ~750 OPF invocations (each emits 2 lines: scanning + completed/failure)\n- **284 parse failures** = 19% of OPF calls couldn't parse the response\n- **Still running** when killed — even with the has-space gate, processing the full fixture would have taken ~25 minutes\n\n### Two real bugs\n\n**Bug 1 (newly found): multi-line input causes `json.Unmarshal` failure.** When a JSON leaf string contains embedded newlines (e.g., code snippets, multi-paragraph messages), `opf` treats each line as a separate input and emits one JSON object per line — concatenated with no delimiter. Our `json.Unmarshal` errors on the second `{`. Result: OPF silently skips redacting those strings and falls back to layers 1–7.\n\n**Bug 2 (already suspected, now confirmed): per-leaf OPF invocation is too slow even with the gate.** The fixture has hundreds of prose leaf strings (with spaces) and each opf call is ~2s. Total per-commit cost on a realistic transcript: many minutes.\n\n### State of the implementation\n\n- **Logically correct** — tests prove the layers work\n- **Practically slow on realistic transcripts** — even with the gate, condensation on big sessions takes minutes\n- **Has a parse bug on multi-line strings** — OPF silently fails on ~20% of inputs in the fixture and falls back\n\n### Your three questions, answered\n\n1. **\"Was there a transcript?\"** — Yes, Vogon did write one, but the kill happened during `RunPrompt` before condensation could run, so OPF was never invoked in the Vogon test. My \"perf issue\" attribution to that test was speculation, not evidence. The perf probe (separate, controlled) confirms the per-leaf cost IS real, just not what hung Vogon.\n\n2. **\"Can I now test end-to-end?\"** — With the current state, F-style smokes on a real agent session will either (a) eventually complete after several minutes per commit, or (b) silently fall back on multi-line strings. Not a clean demo. Better to fix the two issues first.\n\n3. **\"Does it tell the user it's processing the OPF filter?\"** — Yes. Smoke D proved it: stderr shows `[entire] redaction: openai privacy filter scanning transcript (this may take a few seconds)` then `completed in N.Ns` (or `→ scanning… / ✓ done (N.Ns)` on a TTY). The UX fires correctly. It just fires *a lot* per commit right now.\n\n---\n\n## Recommended next step: batch the OPF call\n\nA surgical fix that addresses both bugs at once:\n\n- Walk the JSON, collect all space-containing leaf strings into one big buffer with a unique line-safe separator (something opf won't split on, like `\\x1f\\x1f\\x1f` if newlines are the problem — or use `-f temp_file` mode which reads the whole file as one input)\n- Make **one** OPF call with the whole batch\n- Map returned spans back to the original leaf positions\n\nCuts per-commit OPF cost from ~minutes to ~3 seconds AND fixes the multi-line parse failure (one input → one JSON output, no concatenation).\n\nThis is real work — probably 100–200 LOC. But it's the right shape before this can be useful on real transcripts.\n\n**Three options for you:**\n\n1. **Ship the batched call now** (~1–2 hours of focused work). Makes the feature actually usable.\n2. **Fix only the newline parse bug** (~15 min — replace `\\n` with a space before sending). Doesn't help perf but stops the silent-fallback. Then document perf as a known limitation.\n3. **Revert the gate, document everything as alpha**, and let users opt in knowing it's slow. Daemon mode becomes the next milestone.\n\nWant me to do (1)?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":969,"cache_read_input_tokens":715430,"output_tokens":1391,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":969,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1391,"cache_read_input_tokens":715430,"cache_creation_input_tokens":969,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":969},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb2hkFKZwC2h9B7XweUin","type":"assistant","uuid":"b40536a8-cdb4-4ac2-8917-17fa1669fdec","timestamp":"2026-05-14T15:32:52.455Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact","sessionId":"fb93c4d8-9548-4a4c-97e6-364245c50453","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"feat/openai-privacy-filter"}
