{"parentUuid":"952ac038-02ed-4ff9-a450-e3b2ef4ab6ec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DooL1DiB6Bj6Z7aQSiFdYm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Run it\n\nIn your fish shell, paste:\n\n```fish\nbash /tmp/smoke-F.sh\n```\n\n## What you should see\n\nThe script does two things:\n\n**1. A real `git commit`** in a throwaway test repo. This goes through Entire's hooks. Since no agent session was started, no condensation runs — OPF doesn't fire here. This just proves the existing pipeline still works with OPF configured (no regressions).\n\n**2. A direct `JSONLBytesWithPrivacyFilter` call** with the greeting file content wrapped as a JSONL message. This is what condensation does internally. You should see:\n\n```\n[entire] redaction: openai privacy filter scanning transcript (this may take a few seconds)\n[entire] redaction: openai privacy filter completed in 3.6s\n--- elapsed: 3.6XXX s ---\n--- redacted output ---\n{\"message\":\"Hello from [REDACTED_PERSON], who lives in San Francisco.\\nThis greeting is also from [REDACTED_PERSON] in Seattle.\\nThe project lead, [REDACTED_PERSON], wrote the original draft.\\n\"}\n```\n\n**Three names**, **one OPF call**, **~3.6s total**.\n\n## To see the progress UX during a real commit\n\nFor that you need a real agent session (claude-code or similar) that creates session transcript data. The flow:\n\n```fish\ncd $TESTREPO  # the test repo from the script above\n# Drive your real agent and mention names in chat:\nentire dispatch ... # if your agent has an entire integration\n# OR just use the agent directly with hooks installed\n# Then:\ngit commit -am \"real session test\"\n```\n\nDuring that `git commit`, you'd see the `[entire] redaction: openai privacy filter scanning transcript…` / `…completed in N.Ns` lines on stderr.\n\n## Known limitation\n\nHuge transcripts (~hundreds of KB of prose total) approach `opf`'s 128K-token context window and may time out. The